# SymbiYosys job for eog_countdown (Verify role, task T1.countdown.fv). Harness: fv_eog_countdown.sv (labels and
# reference semantics there): spec v4 + TASKS.md answers 1, 20, 21, 33, 34.
#   bash scripts/formal.sh countdown                        # the default tasks below
#   cd formal/countdown && sby -f eog_countdown.sby bmc_deep  # opt-in deep tasks (long; see below)
#
# Instance: N_FAC = 2, CD_LOG2 = 2 (ring of 4), RW = 8 (REC_NO low bits), MAX_INFLIGHT 8 (the spec sets no bound;
# the RTL holds <= 4). Port-level facts from the RTL author (not assumed, only used to size depths): latency 55 at
# CD_LOG2 = 2, accept gap 15 with in_valid = out_ready = 1, <= 4 records in flight at II = 16, one at a time at
# II >= 57, reset sweep <= N_FAC + 8 cycles (conventions §1). So the first output of a record accepted after the
# sweep is due around step 11 + 55 = 66, and every value property needs a depth above that.
#
# Arithmetic: `prove*`, `bmc`, `cover`, `bmc_deep`, `cover_wrap` use formal/common/eog_mul_abstract.sv and
# eog_div_abstract.sv (q free except q = all ones when d = 0; out_valid/tag exactly LAT = NW + 1 later). Sound for
# every check except the quotient values; the RTL author confirms that every forced value (tripped 0, q <= 0 ->
# 0xFFFF, non-updating 3 x 0xFFFF, NOT_FILLING) bypasses the divider. `bmc_arith` uses rtl/eog_mul.sv + rtl/eog_div.sv.
#
# Why the split. Per-record value checks compare the output with what the harness captured at accept; a record can
# wait inside the stage for an unbounded time under back-pressure when several are in flight, so they are not
# port-inductive at II = 16. History checks (shadow ring) are never port-inductive. Hence:
#
# prove      (default) k-induction, II = 16 (<= 4 in flight), -DFV_STAGE: the stage contract only:
#            u_out.ax_reset/ax_hold/ax_data, u_stage.st_order/st_no_ghost/st_inflight/st_cnt/st_link_n/st_link_r,
#            f_trk. Uses the RTL's opt-in formal invariant -DEOG_FV_RECNO_SEQ=8 (FIFO entries hold consecutive
#            REC_NOs; true whenever st_recno_in is assumed), which makes st_link_r inductive. Depth 12.
#            II and latency bounds are not in this task (they need depth > 16 / > 128): bmc / bmc_deep.
# bmc_pass   (default) bmc from reset, II = 16 (several records in flight, out_ready free), -DFV_PROVE: the
#            record-local checks with pass-through, PAYLOAD free: H_hdr/H_feat/H_rules (header, FEAT, RULES4
#            copied), C1_cd/C1_nf, C1x_cd/C1x_nf (TASKS #1), C2_cd/C2_nf (#21), C3_hr, C5_nf, C5_q, C5_qbig.
#            Depth 70 > first output (~66). Bounded: per-record checks are not port-inductive at II = 16.
# prove_one  (opt-in, slow: the base case alone passes step 24 after ~10 min on the stub) the same checks as
#            bmc_pass, unbounded: k-induction at II = 64 (the RTL processes one record at a time at II >= 57), so a
#            record is hidden inside the stage for at most its latency (55) and depth 60 closes without RTL
#            invariants. Keeps the u_stage asserts (st_cnt / st_link_* are needed as induction hypotheses).
# bmc        (default) bmc from reset, II = 16, out_ready free: record-local + history (C4_nf, C5_m10/m50/m90
#            on the shadow ring; C1 "no ring change" and C7 slot independence through the per-slot shadow) +
#            u_stage.st_ii (II <= 16 after the sweep). PAYLOAD = 0 (uninterpreted input bits tied to 0; bmc_pass /
#            prove_one check pass-through), INFLOW from 5 bits (q = 0..15, so mean = 0 and > 0 both occur). Depth 85:
#            the outputs of the first two records (fill, then one push or another slot / HIST_RESET / INVALID).
# bmc_arith  (default) bmc from reset, real eog_mul + eog_div, -DFV_ARITH: + C6_p10/p50/p90 (m(q) exact), C5_ord,
#            C3_eq. out_ready = 1 (READY1; the arithmetic does not depend on back-pressure), operands narrowed
#            structurally: INFLOW 5 bits, LEVEL 11 bits signed, K_CD < 2^15, SHUT_LVL < 2^10 (K·Δ up to 2^26, so
#            the 0xFFFF clamp, finite values and tripped records all occur). Depth 85 (as bmc).
# cover      (default) cover goals cv_trip, cv_nf, cv_fin, cv_mix, cv_inv, cv_drop, cv_oob, cv_bp, cv_refill
#            (assertions removed; cv_wrap is in cover_wrap). Depth 85.
# bmc_deep   (opt-in) as bmc with out_ready = 1 and depth 135: C4/C5 across a wrapped ring (fill + 4 pushes of one
#            slot = 5 records x 15 cycles + 55) and u_stage.st_lat (latency <= 128, needs depth > 128 + sweep).
# cover_wrap (opt-in) cv_wrap (a ring whose prefilled values are all gone) and the other goals except cv_bp
#            (out_ready = 1 here), depth 135.
# The spec's "a ring that has wrapped" cover and the wrapped-ring history are only reachable at depth ~130, which
# costs about a minute per step on this pipeline; the default tasks stop at 85 and the bit-exact simulation
# (tb/countdown, every vector case incl. Mudit's golden sets) covers wrapped rings.
#
# Run times against a throwaway stub (P = 4, gap 15, latency 55; never committed) on the shared WSL box are in the
# T1.countdown.fv report.

[tasks]
prove: default
bmc: default
bmc_pass: default
bmc_arith: default
cover: default
prove_one
bmc_deep
cover_wrap

[options]
prove:      mode prove
prove:      depth 12
prove_one:  mode prove
prove_one:  depth 60
bmc:        mode bmc
bmc:        depth 85
bmc_pass:   mode bmc
bmc_pass:   depth 70
bmc_arith:  mode bmc
bmc_arith:  depth 85
cover:      mode cover
cover:      depth 85
bmc_deep:   mode bmc
bmc_deep:   depth 135
cover_wrap: mode cover
cover_wrap: depth 135

[engines]
prove:      smtbmc yices
prove_one:  smtbmc yices
bmc:        abc bmc3
bmc_pass:   abc bmc3
bmc_arith:  abc bmc3
cover:      smtbmc yices
bmc_deep:   abc bmc3
cover_wrap: smtbmc yices

[script]
prove:      read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_STAGE -DEOG_FV_RECNO_SEQ=8 eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
prove_one:  read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_PROVE eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
bmc_pass:   read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_PROVE eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
bmc:        read_verilog -formal -sv -I .            eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
bmc_arith:  read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_ARITH eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul.sv eog_div.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
cover:      read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_COVER eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
bmc_deep:   read_verilog -formal -sv -I .            eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
cover_wrap: read_verilog -formal -sv -I . -DFV_COVER eog_fv_props.sv eog_mul_abstract.sv eog_div_abstract.sv eog_countdown.sv fv_eog_countdown.sv
prove:      chparam -set II_CHK 0 -set LAT_CHK 0 fv_eog_countdown
prove_one:  chparam -set II 64 -set II_CHK 0 -set LAT_CHK 0 fv_eog_countdown
bmc:        chparam -set PAYLOAD 0 -set N_IB 5 -set LAT_CHK 0 fv_eog_countdown
bmc_pass:   chparam -set II_CHK 0 -set LAT_CHK 0 fv_eog_countdown
bmc_arith:  chparam -set PAYLOAD 0 -set READY1 1 -set N_IB 5 -set N_LB 11 -set N_KB 15 -set N_SB 10 -set II_CHK 0 -set LAT_CHK 0 fv_eog_countdown
cover:      chparam -set PAYLOAD 0 -set N_IB 5 fv_eog_countdown
bmc_deep:   chparam -set PAYLOAD 0 -set READY1 1 -set N_IB 5 fv_eog_countdown
cover_wrap: chparam -set PAYLOAD 0 -set READY1 1 -set N_IB 5 fv_eog_countdown
prep -top fv_eog_countdown
prove_one:  chformal -assert -remove *eog_fv_axis
bmc_pass:   chformal -assert -remove *eog_fv_stage *eog_fv_axis
bmc:        chformal -assert -remove *eog_fv_axis *eog_fv_stage/st_order *eog_fv_stage/st_no_ghost *eog_fv_stage/st_inflight *eog_fv_stage/st_cnt *eog_fv_stage/st_link_n *eog_fv_stage/st_link_r
bmc_arith:  chformal -assert -remove *eog_fv_stage *eog_fv_axis
cover:      chformal -assert -remove
cover:      chformal -cover -remove fv_eog_countdown/cv_wrap
bmc_deep:   chformal -assert -remove *eog_fv_axis *eog_fv_stage/st_order *eog_fv_stage/st_no_ghost *eog_fv_stage/st_inflight *eog_fv_stage/st_cnt *eog_fv_stage/st_link_n *eog_fv_stage/st_link_r
cover_wrap: chformal -assert -remove
cover_wrap: chformal -cover -remove fv_eog_countdown/cv_bp
setundef -anyseq

[files]
../common/eog_fv_props.sv
../common/eog_mul_abstract.sv
eog_div_abstract.sv
../../rtl/eog_defs.svh
../../rtl/eog_mul.sv
../../rtl/eog_div.sv
../../rtl/eog_countdown.sv
fv_eog_countdown.sv
